+# dp, 2026-10-24: "if a specific path is reachable via an explicit grant, then that grant prevails
+# for that path (basically standing as separate governance path from nested). for paths with no
+# direct grant, the shortest nested grant applies" -- "if explicit grant, use explicit grant; else
+# traverse to ../ and repeat". Part B admitted a path through ANY covering grant (a union), so an
+# `r` grant on `a/b/**` beneath a full `a/**` admitted writes to `a/b`: the narrowing an operator
+# chose was silently widened by a broader grant above it. Here every grant is a NODE; the deepest
